          "title": "DOP \u2014 satellite geometry quality (tDOP is the one for timing)",
          "description": "Dilution of precision. tDOP is the timing-specific geometry factor \u2014 even with strong sats, bad sky geometry hurts PPS accuracy. <1 = excellent, 1\u20132 = good, 2\u20135 = acceptable, >5 = poor. Recurring tDOP spikes at the same time of day usually mean an antenna sees only part of the sky.",
          "datasource": {
